 The difficulty of the timing will be—. I don''t know the number of records that some of these local authority data sets hold. We had, sort of, 60,000 records in some data sets, others had 80, some may only have had 8,000. So, it really will depend on the decision of the EROs as to what data sets they request. We, obviously, started the process quite early, in that we started looking at data sets—some were discarded because they weren''t of good enough quality or didn''t have the sufficient information we needed. But I think eight weeks should be enough for most of the teams. Even those large local authorities, who will have much bulkier data sets, will have, probably, a larger team to help cope with that and the funding to try and support that. Also, there''s some work being done now in the next week or two with the AEA to share some knowledge and good practice from local authorities that currently do a lot of data matching and data cleaning. So, hopefully, sharing those skills to be able to roll that out will be helpful.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Sandra Matthews', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=5577&l=en', NULL, 69.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.452848', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770021', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 Strengthening the private rented sector is a priority for this Government. I think we''ve made that pretty clear; we set it out in my legislative statement on 14 July. Renters in Wales deserve a safe, warm, secure and affordable home and should feel confident challenging poor conditions. Positive change requires good law, and in the first phase of our legislative programme we''ll deliver legislation that protects tenants and tackles poor landlords, making renting, hopefully, more secure.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16260', '2026-09-15', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16260', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16260?startPos=2157&l=en', NULL, 82.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'private_rented_sector; fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context; Private rented sector', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'landlords; legislative programme; private rented; private rented sector; renters', 0, '2026-09-19T12:39:25.121307', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16260&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769001', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 So, we see pressures coming from Bay 32, in terms of the plans that we have for the estate; we see pressures emanating from incorporating the impact or the outcomes of Senedd reform into the baseline; and we foresee different pressures emanating from energy and fuel costs, and the sorts of things that affect our costs from year to year. And in that context, we couple that with an overview of our workforce, because our workforce accounts for more than two thirds of the costs that we can control. And so it''s very important that we have the correct level, a level that allows our staff to have a level of personal well-being and to be industrious within their ability, but is not too many staff members. So that is something that we look at and manage dynamically from year to year.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16295', '2026-10-08', 'Manon Bonner', '', '', '', '', 'Finance Committee', '3. Scrutiny of the Senedd Commission Draft Budget 2027-28: Evidence Session', '16295', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16295?startPos=1110&l=en', NULL, 86.2, 'High', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context; committee_scrutiny', 'Context; Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Finance Committee; draft budget; evidence session', 0, '2026-10-09T13:34:37.055661', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16295&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#777239', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

