 Raising awareness of the UPRN number, raising awareness of, perhaps, having a certain standard when you enter somebody''s name and certain fields that should be a must, I think, will develop over time. Again, one of the reasons we wanted to pilot is to see and to test data sets. We often hear from electors, ''Well, I''ve told council tax, I''ve told one of your other departments''—I''m sure you know, you often hear it—and yet we don''t have this joined-up approach. So, moving forward, there is definitely an opportunity where somebody has contacted the local authority, as they do for registrars with Tell Us Once, that works seamlessly and hopefully alleviates the problem, where somebody has passed away, that, actually, they don''t need to contact 10 other departments where that person, an individual, might show up on. So, I think it''s longer term, but it''s not going to happen overnight. You''ve probably been aware with local authorities that these things do take time to bed in, and encouragement, even, from you to local authorities to work on this, moving forward, would help.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Sandra Matthews', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=5686&l=en', NULL, 109.2, 'High', 'digest', 'taxation_of_property; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Tax & finance', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; council tax; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.469851', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769928', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
