 The Welsh Government previously had two strategies: the carrot of offering money for people to bring homes up to a better standard so they could be sold, and the stick of charging additional council tax. If people still refused, then there are compulsory purchase orders, which are incredibly difficult, incredibly expensive, and nowhere near as certain as some of those who shout it out as a solution actually understand. But do you think those things done so far are helping, or are they just barely touching the surface?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16305', '2026-10-01', 'Mike Hedges', '', '332', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '5. Follow-up inquiry into Empty Properties: Evidence session 3', '16305', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16305?startPos=15238&l=en', NULL, 235.7, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'taxation_of_property; planning_system; local_government_enforcement; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Planning & place; Tax & finance', 'Opposition housing leads', 'Consultation open; Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; compulsory purchase; council tax; empty properties; evidence session; inquiry; planning permission', 0, '2026-10-07T06:31:26.661256', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16305&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#775374', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 As I''ve come in, I''m pleased to find Derwyn in post, but we''re asking ourselves again, ''Do we need to make further changes to bolster our skills, tackle that issue even more and add more capacity there?'' I think it''s a really important aspect of our work in Audit Wales. I think, as we move into the discussions about our new strategy and future, this is something that we''ll be doing more and more of. So, I think it was a good first step to make those changes to the executive leadership team, and it''s definitely bringing a different focus to us in our discussions.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16294', '2026-10-01', 'Catherine Mealing-Jones', '', '', '', '', 'Finance Committee', '3. Audit Wales - Scrutiny of Annual Report and Accounts 2025-26 and the Annual Plan 2026-27: Evidence Session 1', '16294', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16294?startPos=1560&l=en', NULL, 86.2, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Delivery bodies', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Finance Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-10-02T12:57:51.028912', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16294&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#774125', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 Research by Wrexham.com shows that, whilst the Plaid Government was questioning the need and rationale for an extra £100 million to be spent on additional learning needs, it was at the very same time asking councils how much more they''d be spending on additional learning needs this year. Now, the data was published just before the supplementary budget vote on your own website.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16262', '2026-09-22', 'Ken Skates', 'Leader of Welsh Labour', '267', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16262', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16262?startPos=1139&l=en', NULL, 66.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet; Opposition housing leads', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-09-23T11:54:34.360849', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16262&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770739', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
