 And then, there are things, as I''ve said, that we can do through legislation, and actively exploring different measures for regulating increases in rent, for example, effectively is really important. We can look at what''s happening in Scotland. Catalonia—there are learnings from there too. It''s important that we look at what works well, and also look at potential drawbacks. But significant steps need considerable policy development, evidence gathering,', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16260', '2026-09-15', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16260', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16260?startPos=2336&l=en', NULL, 66.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'housing_supply; social_housing', 'Housing system; Planning & place', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'social homes; social housing', 0, '2026-09-16T11:53:07.221987', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16260&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769022', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

