 On the potential reforms—and these are my own personal opinions—of some of the land transaction tax, reliefs tied to bringing long-term properties back into use are certainly advantageous. The council tax A and C exemptions, as long as they are quite tightly managed, certainly seem appropriate and fitting in order to try to incentivise developers to bring these properties back into use, or to try to get them moved on to another owner.

 Incentives linked to occupation and improvement, and targeted relief for regeneration areas, are all worthy of consideration, but we do have to bear in mind that market forces still have a part to play in this in certain areas of Wales. Where an economy in a locality has resulted in a strong housing demand, then it''s much easier to bring the properties back into use. And something I would say is that, if you''ve got an area with significantly reduced housing demand, punishing the owners of properties that are very keen to bring them back into use with extra costs around their empty status significantly burdens people who are already struggling to bring these properties back into use, and so that''s something that does need to be weighed evenly.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16305', '2026-10-01', 'Dr Henry Dawson', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. Follow-up inquiry into Empty Properties: Evidence session 1', '16305', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16305?startPos=2449&l=en', NULL, 189.7, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'taxation_of_property; committee_scrutiny; named_welsh_legislation', 'Context; Housing system; Tax & finance', '', 'Consultation open; Opportunity to influence', 'Land Transaction Tax; Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; council tax; council tax premiums; empty properties; evidence session; inquiry; land transaction tax', 0, '2026-10-07T06:31:25.150245', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16305&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#775309', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 On Cynnal, it''s a really good example. We know what we''re trying to do with Cynnal. There are practical difficulties with implementing it because we don''t have the powers. Again, a good example of why we need the tools at our disposal. But we think we''ve found a way of doing it: we''re going to pilot it. The working group has already met four times. It''s not something that we''re planning how we''re going to address this. It is happening, guided by my Deputy First Minister. I''m not going to apologise for thinking out carefully how we make decisions that will improve the lives of people in Wales.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16262', '2026-09-22', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '4. Statement by the First Minister: ''New Ambition for Wales: Programme for Government 2026-2030''', '16262', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16262?startPos=11551&l=en', NULL, 99.0, 'High', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', 'Decision or commitment; Opportunity to influence', 'programme for government; we have decided; working group', 0, '2026-09-26T13:20:20.156453', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16262&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771019', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 Last week, Labour, you voted with Reform to ensure that this Senedd voted against fair funding for Wales. Labour voted against fair funding for Wales. I shudder to think how successive successful previous Labour First Ministers would have viewed that. Today, you vote against £120 million for ALN provision in Wales, with Reform. You will be voting with parties of the right, who will welcome you. [ Interruption .] Hear them. Hear them. They will welcome you with open arms, because you will give them their majority today. And you are doing so against a progressive budget that provides more support for those most in need in Wales.

 The fine statue of Rhodri Morgan is tonight watching its first vote in this Senedd since it was unveiled. I served as a Minister in his Government. He reflected the progressive co-operative values of the Labour Party in Wales. Today, Labour have abandoned those values. And in these final few moments before the vote, there is still time for you to reclaim them. Reclaim them.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16085', '2026-07-14', 'Elin Jones', '', '162', '', '', 'Plenary', '9. Debate: The First Supplementary Budget 2026-27', '16085', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16085?startPos=26318&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-08-04T14:03:10.849227', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16085&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#768005', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

