 So, there are a few things that we''re looking at. There''s being more flexible, so having central resource being deployed where Ministers want people deployed, introducing more specialism as a principle. So, we specialise. I''ve been doing this job for 15 years and, naturally, if you''re doing it for that long, you get better at it, if you''re doing nothing else. So, we''re looking to see how that principle can be adopted in other parts of the organisation. And there''s a lot of potential with technology and the use of AI to try to make things happen more quickly, and perhaps to standardise certain processes. We''re a long way, by the way, away from not needing us as legislative counsel, I''m fairly confident in saying, but at the same time we need to be open-minded and we need to look at how we can use technology to make things faster and better.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Dylan Hughes', '', '', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=834&l=en', NULL, 86.2, 'High', 'digest', 'planning_system; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Planning & place', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee; planning legislation', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.184722', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770403', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 In order to produce a blended budget that can command a Senedd majority, my only plea across the Chamber is that we have a common understanding also of the financial envelope available to us. We are facing the most challenging budget settlement of this decade in 2027-28, with a real-terms reduction of around 0.7 per cent in resource funding, and even greater reductions in capital budgets. The financial envelope for next year''s budget is especially tight, and will require a particular discipline for this Government and for all of us who want to play a constructive part in passing Wales''s annual budget.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16261', '2026-09-16', 'Elin Jones', 'Cabinet Minister for Finance', '162', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Finance', '16261', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16261?startPos=2874&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'supplementary budget', 0, '2026-09-19T12:39:16.903040', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16261&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769514', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 Cabinet Minister, sadly, it''s not just unpaid carers who have been seemingly kicked to the curb by your Government. The programme for government quite rightly makes specific commitments relating to cardiovascular disease, strokes, mental health and diabetes, yet it does not say anything specifically about lung disease, despite it being the third biggest killer here in Wales. Not only that, but Wales has the highest lung disease mortality rate in western Europe. Given the scale of lung disease in Wales, why has it been omitted from the Government''s programme? And what message does this send to the hundreds of thousands of people living with lung conditions who continue to experience some of the worst outcomes anywhere in western Europe? Thank you.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16314', '2026-10-07', 'Natasha Asghar', '', '336', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Health and Care', '16314', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16314?startPos=1411&l=en', NULL, 16.5, 'Noise', 'archive', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', '', '', 'programme for government', 0, '2026-10-07T13:41:36.762861', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16314&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#776651', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
