 The other element of our work is just talking about the children growing up in temporary accommodation and the need for properties. How on earth do you say to them, ''Sorry, we can''t buy that one because the bedroom''s not quite big enough for you'', when, actually, a whole family might be sharing one bed-and breakfast-room tonight. Just the whole—. ''Yes, definitely'', is the answer to that one.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16305', '2026-10-01', 'Wendy Dearden', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '5. Follow-up inquiry into Empty Properties: Evidence session 3', '16305', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16305?startPos=16001&l=en', NULL, 270.2, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'energy_efficiency; taxation_of_property; housing_supply; homelessness; social_housing; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Planning & place; Property & energy; Tax & finance', '', 'Consultation open; Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; Welsh housing quality standard; council houses; empty properties; evidence session; inquiry; social homes; temporary accommodation', 0, '2026-10-07T06:31:26.795021', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16305&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#775384', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
