 I think what does reassure me and what I am reassured by, though, is that, last year, we upheld 5 per cent of those reviews. That means, in 5 per cent of the reviews, we found perhaps we had missed something or we did need to go back and reopen and relook at part of that case. So, it''s a very small proportion, and we''ve been pretty consistent with that figure over the last few years. So, I''m reassured by that. So, I think we need to just accept that people have the right to ask for a review. We are also looking at how we do that process, again, trying to make it a bit more efficient, so that it''s not so resource intensive, but we give people that review that they''ve asked for.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16295', '2026-10-08', 'Michelle Morris', '', '', '', '', 'Finance Committee', '6. Public Services Ombudsman for Wales- Annual Report and Accounts 2025-26, and Estimate 2027-28: Evidence session', '16295', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16295?startPos=8180&l=en', NULL, 69.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Finance Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-10-09T13:34:37.891237', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16295&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#777613', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

