 We feel as though those premiums should be applied only in circumstances where empty homes teams are there to support owners out of that circumstance. We do feel as though they work in terms of providing the disincentive for owners, but, conversely, they also work as an incentive for councils to not do much empty homes work because they''re generating more money. Certainly, in England, we''re seeing more and more councils take that position. 

 It has to find the balance. It has to find the right balance. On whether they are working in general, the empty homes premiums have been in place and applicable now for a number of years, and yet the empty homes numbers have only ever increased. So, whether they are providing the right incentive for owners, we don''t know. Whether they''re providing the incentive more now for councils is yet to be seen, but it is another tool, it is another option, it is another opportunity for councils, and we just need more of them. We need more solutions.

 Like I said earlier, each solution that we can provide probably only targets 5 per cent of the overall numbers. With funding streams, we''re looking at bringing 5 per cent of all empty homes back into use. With council tax, and council tax premiums, second homes premiums, we''re again looking at probably 5 per cent. So, it is a case of needing more solutions and more opportunities, but it all starts with a council having a dedicated officer in post.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16305', '2026-10-01', 'Adam Cliff', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. Follow-up inquiry into Empty Properties: Evidence session 1', '16305', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16305?startPos=2545&l=en', NULL, 195.5, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'taxation_of_property; second_homes_and_short_term_lets; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Planning & place; Tax & finance', '', 'Consultation open; Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; council tax; council tax premiums; empty homes; empty properties; evidence session; inquiry; second homes', 0, '2026-10-07T06:31:25.164352', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16305&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#775317', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

