 It is a consultation on how the planning process needs to be made more effective and efficient, but it is also a consultation on our long-term vision for Wales. The reason for doing this is that we feel that, during the existence of this Senedd, a clear direction in terms of the future of our nation hasn''t been adequately apparent. So, there is an opportunity, with a new Government, to use the process that exists in statute already, namely the reform of the national planning framework, to have that conversation with the people of Wales on the long-term future of our nation.

 Plaid Cymru firmly believes in building Wales, in building the nation, and creating a Wales that works for the people of Wales, connecting Wales more effectively in terms of transport, for example. That isn''t happening at the moment, as anyone who travels around our country will know. We are not well connected, so transport comes into this consultation.

 There is an opportunity to discuss energy policy too. We know that we are facing challenges in moving forward with more renewable energy developments. So, under this framework, there are a number of different plans that will sit underneath it. And I understand the comments that you make about plans and strategies, and so on, and I share some of that frustration. What we want is action, to see things happening. But they have to happen in a co-ordinated way and in a way that has been properly discussed in terms of the long-term direction of travel that we want to see for our nation. I don''t think that ''Future Wales'', the current plan, provides that clear picture as to what kind of future Wales needs. And certainly, ''Future Wales'', the existing plan, hasn''t been able to identify some of the major challenges, some of which are developing as we speak, of course, because the plan is old, and there are new challenges coming to face us all the time and we must, therefore, reform in order to take into account all those other issues that are part of our vision for developing our nation. Thank you.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16264', '2026-09-29', 'Sian Gwenllian', '', '4981', '', '', 'Plenary', '5. Statement by the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning: The Revision of the National Development Framework and National Conversation', '16264', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16264?startPos=8537&l=en', NULL, 104.5, 'High', 'digest', 'planning_system', 'Planning & place', 'Housing minister', 'Consultation open', 'Future Wales; consultation; planning applications; planning system', 0, '2026-10-03T13:38:59.002164', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16264&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#772995', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

