 So, I''m not seeking to avoid the question or—give the assurance that we want people to feel that, if we''re saying this outcome needs to be achieved, we''ll have a very real conversation as to how and what that means in financial terms, but it should never be just because the size of the budget always needs to increase. So, I''d caution against committing to that, but if we can have a proper conversation at all times around what ''fully funded'' means, then that''s a more realistic conversation for me to have, rather than just about size of budgets.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16294', '2026-10-01', 'Elin Jones', '', '162', '', '', 'Finance Committee', '6. Welsh Government Draft Budget 2027-28 - Pre-budget scrutiny: Cabinet Minister for Finance', '16294', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16294?startPos=9201&l=en', NULL, 74.8, 'Medium', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context; committee_scrutiny', 'Context; Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Finance Committee; draft budget', 0, '2026-10-02T12:57:51.970630', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16294&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#774496', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 So, we started—it''s a good two or three years ago now—looking for staff where we knew there was already an evidenced need to prepare for Senedd reform, and we could foresee that there would definitely be a need for more members of staff on our side who could be preparing for the intake of the new Members when they arrived. But beyond that, we have, through a system of annual service planning, kept together by the corporate plan, which is within the medium-term resourcing framework—I''m sorry to use all these words, but just to explain the levels of assurance that we go through—we have not gone ahead and recruited staff until there is evidence of need, so we''ve waited until decisions have been taken. We still have some staff within that total that have not yet been recruited, because we have been waiting for the Senedd to take final decisions on the pattern of business and how many more committees there might be, or whether there''s an extra Plenary; that sort of decision.

 So, we''ve tried to strike a balance throughout on getting staff in place to serve the Senedd, which is our core job as Commission staff, but not go ahead of evidenced need. And in that, we have each year been scrutinised by the predecessor of this committee. We''ve then been scrutinised in terms of the previous year''s budgets by the Public Accounts and Public Administration Committee. We also have several lines of insurances, including our audit and risk committee, which is made up of independent people who are all expert in their fields and, of course, the Commission itself, to whom I report.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16295', '2026-10-08', 'Manon Bonner', '', '', '', '', 'Finance Committee', '3. Scrutiny of the Senedd Commission Draft Budget 2027-28: Evidence Session', '16295', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16295?startPos=1262&l=en', NULL, 86.2, 'High', 'digest', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context; committee_scrutiny', 'Context; Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Finance Committee; draft budget; evidence session', 0, '2026-10-09T13:34:37.075635', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16295&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#777478', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 There are a few Members who want to pick up some more questions. Sera, there are a couple more bits from your side. One second, Elfed, before you come in, I just want to get the order of things organised here. So it''ll be Sera, then Lyn and then Huw. But before that, you want to come in on this particular point, Elfed, yes?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16294', '2026-10-01', 'Sam Rowlands', '', '8734', '', '', 'Finance Committee', '3. Audit Wales - Scrutiny of Annual Report and Accounts 2025-26 and the Annual Plan 2026-27: Evidence Session 1', '16294', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16294?startPos=1995&l=en', NULL, 97.7, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Other committee chairs; Delivery bodies', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Finance Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-10-02T12:57:51.107994', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16294&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#774225', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 The challenge for us now is in terms of travel. That is where our carbon reduction still needs some reduction. But there is a balance to be struck between the need to travel for things like audit-quality purposes and for things like the development of a team spirit, working with colleagues, which is really, really important, but we''ve got to make sure that we travel only when necessary. So, the things that we are looking at this year—. As you''ll see from our annual plan, we''ve actually changed our target to a further 25 tonne reduction, and we''ve been working with staff to see how we can achieve that. It equates to something like reducing travel by car by about 10 per cent to 15 per cent—so, swapping a car journey for active travel or public transport—but also things like, in the winter, turning the heating down by a degree or so, or, in the summer, not putting the air conditioning on quite so much. So, we''re really looking to engage with staff right across the organisation to help us to meet what is still, as Catherine said, a stretching target. But we think that that 25 tonne target, for example, this year is achievable.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16294', '2026-10-01', 'Kevin Thomas', '', '', '', '', 'Finance Committee', '3. Audit Wales - Scrutiny of Annual Report and Accounts 2025-26 and the Annual Plan 2026-27: Evidence Session 1', '16294', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16294?startPos=466&l=en', NULL, 86.2, 'High', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'Delivery bodies', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Finance Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-10-02T12:57:50.795454', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16294&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#774460', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 One other point I''d make is that there are certain things that are within our gift. The choice of the UK Government about when to produce legislation and how effectively they''ve co-operated with us in terms of their timetables is another matter, which I have little ability to influence wholly at the moment. Again, I have raised some of these issues with Hamish Falconer, my opposite number in the Cabinet Office in the UK Government, and there is at least an acknowledgement of the issues and a stated desire to work together. So, I hope that''ll be reflected in practice too.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16254', '2026-09-21', 'Dafydd Trystan Davies', '', '12140', '', '', 'Legislation Committee', '3. General Scrutiny session with the Counsel General and the Cabinet Minister for Government Effectiveness and the Constitution', '16254', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16254?startPos=1009&l=en', NULL, 57.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'Legislation Committee', 0, '2026-09-22T11:55:09.215061', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16254&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770413', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 Resilience—I talked about this last week—is an issue that I have tried to focus a great deal on since I came into the role of First Minister, understanding the various elements that contribute to the resilience, or lack of, in some ways, that we have as a society. Wildfires happen to be the one that has grabbed our attention, which is why we need to make sure that we''re tightening up those resilience elements around that in the summit on 22 October. But the Member is right; flooding is something that many communities will be concerned about. There are other concerns too—the effects of heat, the effects of cold and so on.

 It is something that we work across the UK on. I want to ensure (a) that Wales gets its fair share of resilience funding, civil contingency funding, across the UK, and that''s something I''m eager to pursue. But the Member has my word that I will absolutely be looking at how we work between Welsh Government and UK Government to get the support that Wales needs to prepare for this wide range of threats that we face in future.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16262', '2026-09-22', 'Rhun ap Iorwerth', 'First Minister of Wales', '2717', '', '', 'Plenary', '1. Questions to the First Minister', '16262', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16262?startPos=1834&l=en', NULL, 38.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'fiscal_and_legislative_context', 'Context', 'First Minister / Cabinet', '', 'programme for government', 0, '2026-09-26T13:20:18.856640', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16262&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#770730', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

