 I think, in terms of the reliance on manual systems, when a human is responsible for doing those data checks, there''s always that element of risk and error and things as well. And I think our biggest concern is that, if this process appears to be rushed in any way, shape or form, or sufficient time is not given to allow for people to do the work correctly, there''s the risk of adding people incorrectly to the register, because those checks haven''t been done fully or properly. It''s the impact that that has long term on the integrity of the process and on the delivery of elections going forward as well.

 And I think, again, it''s also those concerns around the access to information as well. We''re very much aware that a lot of authorities in Wales are currently struggling to access the local data sources. They need to do this exercise. There are regulations, but the regulations that are relied upon that allow electoral registration officers access to things have always been a barrier. UK Government have recognised this and they''re currently, in the Representation of the People Bill, trying to address that to make sure those barriers don''t exist. And it''s a shame that Welsh Government haven''t carried out those things first to allow greater access to those data sources to take away some of those barriers that currently exist as well. So, again, it''s about having that time period to make sure that the legislative framework and the digital framework are in place to successfully allow for what could be a really successful initiative to get more people on the register and to exercise their democratic rights.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16256', '2026-09-17', 'Clare Sim', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '3. The Representation of the People (Electoral Registration without Applications) (Electoral Reform) (Wales) Regulations 2026: Evidence session 2', '16256', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16256?startPos=4224&l=en', NULL, 69.0, 'Medium', 'digest', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', 'Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; evidence session', 0, '2026-09-18T11:33:49.219376', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16256&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#769932', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
