 We know the public sector very much has a big part to play. We saw some statistics this week about the benefits being brought by electric vehicle fleets within the public sector, saving millions and millions of pounds to taxpayers because of the benefits that they bring. So, we''re on that journey. I want to continue on that trajectory. And I know local government are keen to as well, because they see much of this as an invest-to-save piece as much as anything else. Whilst there very often is quite considerable capital investment upfront, you can then start realising some of those savings. So, that is something I absolutely want to do.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16233', '2026-09-23', 'Llyr Gruffydd', '', '425', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', '2. General scrutiny of the Cabinet Minister for Rural Resilience and Sustainability', '16233', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16233?startPos=4773&l=en', NULL, 34.5, 'Low', 'dashboard', 'committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system', '', '', 'Climate Change, Environment, Sustainability and Rural Affairs Committee', 0, '2026-09-25T06:30:34.925525', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16233&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#771786', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 We find the proactive identification of properties nearly impossible. We tend to buy our properties from auction at a point where a seller''s gone through that process and wanted to sell and move on, and the consequence of that is that we know little about that property and what''s come before. So, having someone to get a database in place that is aligned to that need and the use of the property rather than the secondary purpose of taxation would be very useful. That was the point I just jumped in on from earlier.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16305', '2026-10-01', 'Trystan Jones', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '5. Follow-up inquiry into Empty Properties: Evidence session 3', '16305', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16305?startPos=14808&l=en', NULL, 155.2, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'taxation_of_property; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Tax & finance', '', 'Consultation open; Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; empty properties; evidence session; inquiry', 0, '2026-10-07T06:31:26.588818', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16305&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#775395', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
