 Also, can I call for a statement from the Welsh Government Cabinet Secretary responsible for social justice and equality on the action being taken by the Welsh Government to address antisemitism in Wales? As we all know, tomorrow marks the third anniversary of those barbaric attacks by Hamas and Islamic Jihad terrorists against Israeli citizens. All of us have condemned those attacks, and what we need to make sure is that Wales is taking appropriate action to address the rise in antisemitism that we''ve seen in our country since.

 One positive action that the previous Welsh Government took, of course, was to recognise the International Holocaust Remembrance Alliance''s definition of antisemitism, and I''d be grateful if the Welsh Government could reaffirm its commitment to that definition so that we can be sure that the same action will be taken by this new Welsh Government as the previous one in terms of providing some leadership on that issue.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16313', '2026-10-06', 'Darren Millar', '', '171', '', '', 'Plenary', '3. Business Statement and Announcement', '16313', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16313?startPos=6732&l=en', NULL, 71.5, 'Medium', 'digest', 'planning_system', 'Planning & place', '', 'Consultation open', 'consultation; permitted development', 0, '2026-10-09T13:35:10.093916', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16313&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#776056', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
