 If they live abroad, that''s not a particular problem as well. As long as we serve it at the Land Registry address, then we''ve got good service. But, again, it''s having the knowledge to have the confidence in the guidance in relation to that. If you''ve got any particular case in mind, I''m happy to have a chat.', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Committee/16305', '2026-10-01', 'Andrew Lavender', '', '', '', '', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee', '2. Follow-up inquiry into Empty Properties: Evidence session 1', '16305', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16305?startPos=3135&l=en', NULL, 155.2, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'taxation_of_property; committee_scrutiny', 'Housing system; Tax & finance', '', 'Consultation open; Opportunity to influence', 'Local Government, Housing and Planning Committee; empty properties; empty property; evidence session; inquiry', 0, '2026-10-07T06:31:25.251195', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16305&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#775323', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

 Whilst every town and city centre has its own unique identity, many are facing the similar challenge of changing footfall and empty properties. That''s why the Welsh Labour Government''s Transforming Towns programme boosted regeneration in town and city centres across Wales, with more than £300 million since 2020. Instead of confirming a continuation of this programme, Cabinet Minister, you''ve created a town-centre taskforce, and I''ve no doubt that the two co-chairs and 17 members announced last week have vast expertise. But I''d like to know what the Government expects of the taskforce and what it expects to deliver. How will the taskforce differ from previous reviews and recommendations, when will it report and how much will it cost to convene the town-centre taskforce?', 'https://record.senedd.wales/Plenary/16314', '2026-10-07', 'Jayne Bryant', '', '5038', '', '', 'Plenary', '2. Questions to the Cabinet Minister for Local Government, Housing and Planning', '16314', 'http://www.senedd.tv/en/16314?startPos=6361&l=en', NULL, 143.0, 'Critical', 'immediate', 'private_rented_sector; taxation_of_property', 'Private rented sector; Tax & finance', 'Housing minister; Opposition housing leads', '', 'empty properties; landlords', 0, '2026-10-10T14:39:12.589115', 'https://record.senedd.wales/XMLExport/Download?meetingID=16314&xmlDownloadType=EnglishTranscript#776712', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
